course: dictionary
lesson: 4413
title: Hallway: a long passage with doors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hallway is a long, narrow passage inside a building, with doors that open into rooms. You walk along a hallway to get somewhere; you do not stay in it.
explain: Context clues help. «Down the hallway» tells you it is a route you travel along, and «at the end of the hallway» tells you it has two ends, so it has length. In «A photo hung in the hallway», the word hallway tells you where the photo is.
explain: A hallway can also mean the space just inside the front door of a house, where you might hang your coat. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits: a passage with rooms off it, or the space by the front door.
fact: A hallway is a long, narrow passage inside a building, with doors to rooms.
fact: A hallway can also be the space just inside the front door of a house.
fact: «Down the hallway» means along the passage, and «at the end of the hallway» means at its far end.
fact: Hallways must be kept clear for fire exits, so that people can get out quickly.
fact: «E-bike batteries must be charged only with the right charger, on a hard surface, and not overnight in a bedroom or hallway.»
exercise: «A photo that once made everyone cry, like Jayden's grandad in the hallway, can one day make them smile.» Where was Jayden's grandad in the photo? | At school | On the beach | In the garden | *In the hallway
exercise: «Keep the hallway clear so that everyone can reach the fire exit.» Why must the hallway be kept clear? | So visitors can see the paintings | So the floor can be cleaned | So the cat can sleep there | *So people can get out quickly in a fire
exercise: «Dad hung the coats in the hallway.» What does hallway mean here? | *The space just inside the front door of a house | A type of bus | A kitchen cupboard | A large, open field
test: «E-bike batteries must not be charged overnight in a bedroom or hallway.» Why is a hallway a place to be careful with? | *A hallway is an escape route, and a fault there could block people getting out | Batteries are scared of the dark | Hallways are always wet | Hallways are too small to hold a charger
test: «She walked down the hallway to her bedroom.» What is a hallway in this sentence? | A staircase going up to the roof | A room with a big window | A small garden at the front of a house | *A long narrow passage inside a building, with doors to rooms
exam: «Dad waited in the hallway while Mia put on her shoes.» Where was Dad waiting? | *Just inside the front door of the house | On the roof | In a shop window | Halfway up a mountain
